OL,3,GNEWSAWildlife and ancient trees
OL,4,Adestroyed by A31 wildfire
OL,5,
OL,6,FAncient oak and beech trees, rare
OL,7,Fheathland and even wetland have been
OL,8,Fdevastated by the recent fire that
OL,9,Fswept through the New Forest, a survey
OL,10,Fhas found.
OL,12,FMore than 1 sq km (247 acres) of the
OL,13,Fnational park has been destroyed since
OL,14,Fthe fire broke out on 9 August,
OL,15,FForestry England said.
OL,17,FThe government agency found areas
OL,18,Fdevoid of vegetation, dead wildlife and
OL,19,Fscorched bogs in an initial inspection
OL,20,Fof the damage.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
